00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.460
It's too damn hot, so let's head down there.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:11.120
The underground! Very shrewd, Kanamori.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.610
I didn't know this was here!

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:16.350
Shibahama gets snowed in during winter, 
so its underground is pretty developed.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.940
It's just a run-down shopping district now.

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:29.790
Th-This...

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.130
Isn't it the legendary spiral 
staircase shopping district,

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:37.040
which is said to reach deep 
into the belly of the earth?!

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.500
<b>Fruit Dandan Noodles</b>

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.500
<b>Fruit Dandan Noodles</b>

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:38.910
Let's eat here.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.980
<b>This week's Special: Fruit Ramen!</b>

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.170
<b>Star Fruit Dandan Noodles:    800 Yen</b>

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:42.170
<b>Banana Dandan Noodles:        POPULAR</b>

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:42.170
<b>Pineapple Dandan Noodles</b>

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:42.170
What the...

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:42.170
<b>Passion fruit Dandan Noodles</b>

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.170
<b>Weekdays Only</b>

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.170
<b>One Free Substitution</b>

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.340
Hey!

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:48.220
You came by!

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:49.230
Hello.

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:50.840
<b>Tsubame Mizusaki</b>

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:50.840
Huh...

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:54.370
That's right! I watched your robot 
anime at the culture festival!

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:55.560
I remember you!

00:06:56.630 --> 00:07:00.600
And afterward, he sent a 
passionate note of praise.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.060
So that's it.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:05.860
Y'know, I watch a fair bit of anime, 
and yours was great! I was moved!

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:08.320
The combination of realistic 
robot design principles

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:11.330
with fantastical super robot action!

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.280
That's the kind of robot anime people 
like me have been waiting for!

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.260
It had the verisimilitude 
that makes you think

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:17.460
the creators knew their stuff!

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.170
And the monster seemed 
like it'd be right at home

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.740
He's actually praising the short.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:20.740
in the Shibahama underground...

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.270
It's incredible you girls managed to 
pull that off while in high school!

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:24.290
I still feel like we've got too much to 
work on to accept it openly, though...

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:24.710
You're prodigies!

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:27.550
This is better than I thought.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:33.520
Yeah, seriously! I didn't think fruit 
would go well with ramen.

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:37.260
Star fruit has a pretty mild flavor, 
so there's pear juice in this.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:39.410
You could even call it pear ramen instead.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:42.220
It goes to show that a dish can be good

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:45.450
even if the fruit used is barely noticeable,
 or bad if you notice it <i>too much</i>.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:46.610
Although part of it being good means

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:50.110
demonstrating what's unique 
about the fruit used.

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:53.530
You never usually go that deep 
with your thoughts about food.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:54.490
I think I get it.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:57.220
Sometimes you need to smother the taste 
of the fruit for it to be good.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:07:59.830
Welcome!

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:03.030
It's probably a little late to point this out, 
but this place is built on an angle, huh?

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:07.240
Right. Supposedly part of the reason 
the noodles are served without broth

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:08.830
is to keep it from spilling out.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:13.430
One pineapple dandan noodles, 
and one dragon fruit dandan noodles!

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:18.460
Just between you and me, I've got 
an incredible idea up my sleeve.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.240
For an anime!

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:23.390
I just have no idea how I'd ever get it made.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:24.700
You wanna hear?

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:25.980
Uh, sure, sure!

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.580
The protagonist is an 
ordinary guy who works at a

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.110
dandan noodle place like this!

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.290
But he has a secret identity...

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:35.950
He's actually an agent with the secret 
police force that protects world peace!

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:40.410
He uses his red pepper bombs 
to fight off an alien invasion!

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:41.660
Coming!

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.660
Sounds good to me. Let's use 
that for our new project.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:48.210
The Yoshidas' place is gonna 
be closing this summer, too.

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.210
It's getting more and more lonely around here.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:55.250
Looks like our film club has a fan!

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.260
There are a lot of deserted storefronts.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:01.470
Not a lot of customers outside of ski season.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:01.470
Don't play in the river by yourself!

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.070
So what are we doing for our next project?

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:05.190
Are we gonna base it on one 
of Asakusa's concepts again?

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:08.050
Last time, we knew from the outset

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:10.610
it was going to be a robot 
versus a giant monster...

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:16.380
The first short had a setting from your 
back catalog of ideas, right, Asakusa?

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:20.780
That was just because we needed 
something fast, so we chose something simple.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.820
And the second time around, 
we used the school.

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:24.860
What've you been doing there, Kanamori?

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:25.660
Making posts.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:28.940
Having fun playing around on
 social media. Must be nice!

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:31.420
There is nothing fun about social media!

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.960
Wait, you're already doing publicity?

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.920
Right. It's better to attract eyes beforehand

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:37.270
than trying to get attention 
around the time of release.

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.180
Say butter.

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:40.720
Wait, what?

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:43.140
Is it all right if I post this?

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.730
Well, sure, if it gets us attention.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:48.150
I've been conscientious about 
likeness rights so far,

00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:50.020
but I'd like to set it up so that

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:53.850
only our followers can view the 
posts with your face in them.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.590
That's fine. My parents 
handle my management anyway.

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:59.090
I really wish people would pay 
attention to our projects and not me, though.

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:01.160
I wouldn't worry about that.

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:04.490
The whole intent is to get people 
to pay attention to the eizouken's output.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:05.940
We get them to develop an emotional attachment,

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:10.190
<b>(Film) Merchandise in the Works</b>

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:08.370
and stimulate their urge to spend money.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:09.170
We're selling merch?

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.860
There's demand for merchandise.

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:16.170
<b>What kind of Eizouken merchandise
 would you want?

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.540
That can be pricey to put together,

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:15.300
but if we measure demand correctly, 
we can avoid risk.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:18.660
We can bust our humps working on a new DVD,
 and it might not sell at 1,000 yen...

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:20.520
But all we need is to 
stamp the club's logo on a

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.620
t-shirt and we can sell <i>that</i> for 2,000 yen.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.550
Even if Tsubame Mizusaki is 
what got them in the doors,

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:28.270
<b>@ACertainProgramDsAccount
 and 76 others liked your post.</b>

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:28.270
the number of people who are genuinely 
interested in our work is increasing.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:29.560
Part of our goal here is to ensure

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:32.950
<b>Film</b>

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:32.950
everyone who watched our last 
project picks this one up, as well.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:35.460
The clips we post might go viral,

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:37.360
giving people an idea of the 
material we're working on...

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.010
Having a large digital footprint can 
help us in a variety of ways.

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:41.730
You're a social media master.

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:47.430
Wow! That's the Mizusaki bump!

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:49.770
I never realized how important 
advertising could be.

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:54.630
Long ago, I bore witness to 
the death of a liquor store!

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:01.820
Fukuya Liquor Store

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:01.820
Fukuya 
Brewery

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:05.750
Is this the liquor store you mentioned?

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:06.710
Seems busy enough.

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.590
My relatives ran it.

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:11.050
It was a drinking spot with a good reputation,

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:12.850
particularly among fans of Japanese sake.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:16.180
But the owner had a high standard for quality,

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:18.660
which did him no favors with the locals

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.510
who just wanted to get hammered at a low price.

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:23.370
That's a shame.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:24.730
The construction of the monorail

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:27.580
meant that the street trolleys 
were done away with,

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:29.360
and since people drove more,
they couldn't drink as much,

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:31.640
<b>Fukuya Liquor Store</b>

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:30.830
leading to even fewer customers...

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:33.050
Which meant less of an emphasis on brewing,

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:34.020
<b>Fukuya Liquor Store</b>

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:36.170
and by the time my uncle was running it,
 they called it a general store.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.300
It's a bit more run down, now.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:42.590
An exemplary general store!

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:44.590
It's so cute!

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:45.650
Look!

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.810
Minimori!

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:57.640
What a hard worker.

00:11:57.640 --> 00:12:00.630
I heard pensions weren't 
enough to get by anymore,

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:03.340
so I was trying to earn money 
apart from just my allowance.

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:08.620
This place looks a lot cleaner! Thank you.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:10.080
Here's a little tip.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:11.580
Thank you very much.

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.950
You should really wait until 
you're home to open it...

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:15.540
There's extra.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:18.260
I wanted to add something special 
since you come by every day.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:21.550
I'm gonna clean some more.

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.990
Old...

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:30.020
<b>Closed</b>

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:33.020
Hello.

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:35.610
Oh my goodness! You're covered in snow!

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:38.340
Did you walk here? That couldn't have been easy!

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:39.980
You're not going to open the store?

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:43.260
No one's gonna be out in this snowstorm.

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:45.530
Even the convenience stores are closed.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:49.630
But people need to buy stuff all the time.

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:52.040
If we open up right now, we'll be
 the only place making money.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.610
I saw footsteps in front 
of the store, too.

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:57.740
Okay, we'll need that snow shoveled, then!

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:58.490
Okay.

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:02.760
You ever notice the kinds of things she does?

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.370
She started shoveling in front of 
the vending machine, for instance...

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:08.430
That means we can start making money 
as soon as that bit of snow is cleared.

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:10.930
Hot drinks sell at times like this.

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:12.770
She really is thoughtful.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.850
She's always got her little eyes open.

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:16.820
Did you know she has trouble with math?

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:19.220
When she's got such a mind for business?

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:20.610
Funny, isn't it?

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:23.220
Thing is, you can be a math wiz, but if
 you don't have a head for business—

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:25.700
the way I don't—it won't matter.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:29.450
It's all clear.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:30.450
Attagirl!

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:33.070
No tip this time.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:35.870
Instead, you can have these. Sell what
 you've got, and make some money.

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:40.630
Man, it's cold.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:41.510
Welcome.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:42.770
Do you have any gloves?

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:46.590
I was thinking about shoveling, 
but all I had were thin rubber ones...

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:49.220
Oh, not like those.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:52.150
I was looking for something nice and thick
 that the snow couldn't soak through.

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:54.580
If you put your rubber gloves on top of these...

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:56.230
Hey, yeah!

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:58.190
Thank you very much.

00:13:58.890 --> 00:14:00.900
Already making a sale!

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:02.890
And you sold a single pair of 
working gloves for 100 yen,

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:04.890
when they're usually a dozen for 300!

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:06.440
Individual sales stack up.

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.060
Hey, you're open!

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:13.970
Welcome.

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:16.670
Hey mister, is the vacant 
lot across from you open?

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:18.220
We were hoping to park there for a bit.

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:19.790
Not a problem.

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.130
Is it all right if we eat in here?

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.000
Make yourself at home.

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:23.960
We have instant noodles.

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:23.960
<b>Soy Ramen</b>

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:25.950
That's perfect! You got hot water?

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:26.610
We do.

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:28.470
Hey, he says it's okay!

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:31.340
<b>20 yen</b>

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:31.340
Man, this is just what I needed!

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:33.850
Can feel myself warming up!

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:34.750
This is good stuff.

00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:41.290
We set out to help folks stuck in 
the snow, but everywhere was closed!

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:50.820
<b></b>

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:45.820
Even the convenience store, and we 
were starving! I thought we might be done for!

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:48.930
I never knew a place like this 
was just across the way...

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:50.820
I'm coming here every week from now on.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:55.160
I appreciate the thought, but we're
 actually closing this month.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.620
What, really?

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:58.960
We've been in the red for a while...

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:00.630
Well, it's not the best location.

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:03.570
You're kinda out of the way and hard to notice,

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:05.650
plus there's a convenience 
store right over there.

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:08.300
It was better when the trains 
were still running, but...

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:10.780
They never finished that damn monorail, either.

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:13.860
How about you only open up on snowy days?

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:15.420
I don't think we could manage that.

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:18.500
Man, if I had known sooner, 
I would've told all my pals!

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:21.460
You let our nasty old cars park outside,
 and you let people stay and eat...

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:22.820
This is a great place.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:25.810
But I guess since everyone going into 
the mountains uses the other road...

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:30.030
Thanks, come again.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:32.410
...well, I guess not.

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:35.910
You're closing even though 
you could get customers?

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:40.910
You need money to even keep a store open.

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:45.220
Heating, repairs, taxes, insurance...

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:48.310
The money to buy stock and have it brought in,

00:15:48.310 --> 00:15:50.920
which goes to waste if anything doesn't sell...

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:53.630
And since we're out of the way, 
customers just don't come by.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:58.850
We've been spending all kinds of money, 
and only surviving off of what was left.

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:02.560
You can't keep a business open with 
only the odd customer here and there.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:05.140
No one's gonna come to a store...

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:07.410
...that nobody knows about.

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:11.440
There's no point in focusing entirely 
on the quality of your product.

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:13.660
You need the right methods
and products at the right time,

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.020
and you need advertising!

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:17.570
If you think a good product is all 
it takes to attract customers,

00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:18.830
you're dreaming!

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:21.010
You can't do business without promotion,

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:23.690
but without a product, 
you can't even get started!

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:24.880
High standards aren't enough!

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:27.890
You also need to think about how 
to loosen people's purse strings!

00:16:27.890 --> 00:16:29.670
And I'll make sure people 
hear about what we make.

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.110
About that...

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:34.850
Last time, we used the Shibahama High campus,

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:38.750
but this time, I'm thinking of basing 
the story in the town itself!

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:42.270
The bizarre terrain and constructions!

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:44.460
A town that's like a watery labyrinth!

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:47.330
Shibahama is a town where you can 
see the remains of trial and error

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:49.150
throughout history, which makes it fascinating!

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:52.820
It's a treasure chest of concepts! 
A 4D pocket dimension full of ideas!

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:55.920
The town comes under attack one day!

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:56.320
<b>Zoom  Screech  Pow</b>

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:57.490
Their enemies are UFOs!

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:57.510
<b>Skeleton</b>

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:58.970
<b>Zap</b>

00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:00.490
Rising to the challenge is the 
anti-invasion weaponry installed

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:00.350
<b>Whoosh

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:01.560
<b>Fiber Laser!
 Powerful!

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:02.270
<b>An armature was added to prevent
 the cord from wrapping around it
 and causing it to fall over,
 but it still does sometimes

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.850
<b>Sci-Fi Ray</b>

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.850
<b>Has a stabilizer like a camera that automatically
 corrects for the turret's shaking

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:01.850
throughout Shibahama!

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:03.890
<b>Directed Energy Weapon</b>

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:03.890
<b>Its suspension absorbs shock</b>

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:03.890
<b>Generator</b>

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:03.890
<b>Uses two mirrors
to generate
a powerful laser</b>

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:03.890
<b>Light Generation</b>

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:03.890
<b>High Intensity Mirror</b>

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:03.890
<b>Low Intensity Mirror</b>

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:03.890
<b>Laser</b>

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:08.230
The spiral shopping district 
rises from the underground!

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
It launches a fleet of steam tanks!

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>m 30 21 l 34 63 107 62 100 26 101 19</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Can emit propulsion
 from any direction 
in order to maintain
 balance</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>This is where it's emitted</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>m 90 157 l 90 213 183 215 200 186 186 162</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Looks like an exterior air conditioner
 but is actually hollow.
 Houses a ducted fan.
Helps with propulsion.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Is able to fly by emitting
 super high-pressure steam</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>m 278 146 l 282 208 350 210 352 174 344 154</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Is able to absorb
 moisture from the air and 
convert it into steam.
 Effective in clouds.</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Dips</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Pressure Gauge</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Some kind
 of piston</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Sit here</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>m 464 177 l 466 218 528 222 521 178</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Landing gear deployed
 when taking off/landing.</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Ducted fan portion (Directs air inward)</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Steam-propelled projected energy
 attack ship that camouflaged and 
stationed throughout the city.</b>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Steam Tank</b>

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.170
<b>Enemy Fortress</b>

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:18.010
<b>Directed energy weapon
 (Fixed)</b>

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:18.430
<b>Wind-Powered</b>

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:17.380
The town of Shibahama was 
outfitted with weaponry!

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:18.430
<b>Directed Energy Weapons</b>

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:18.430
<b>Steam Tanks</b>

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:18.430
<b>Energy Weapon</b>

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:20.780
That's kinda cool!

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:22.000
If we used the town for the setting,

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:23.870
do you think people who live 
here will be more invested?

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:26.190
Can you wrap this up in 30 minutes?

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:27.850
I'm still figuring out the details.

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:30.940
But regardless, we've got the premise 
and setting for our next project figured out!

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:33.230
The eizouken's next project...

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:35.690
is the Shibahama-UFO Battle!

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:39.320
<b>123 Days Until Deadline !</b>

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:58.090
<b>Fruit Dandan Noodles</b>

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:58.090
<b>Fruit Noodles</b>

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:58.090
<b>Closed
Today</b>

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:17.730
By the way, I heard that the student 
council started taking the rent I'm paying.

00:18:17.730 --> 00:18:18.900
Wait, are we gonna be okay?!

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:20.950
What about the budget for the new project?!

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:24.130
I just finalized a deal where the 
Shibahama Chamber of Commerce

00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:26.610
has agreed to fully finance the short.

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:28.390
That's awesome!

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:30.960
How'd you do it?! Was it thuggery?!

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:34.530
Mr. Kashima from the 
dandan noodle shop lent his support.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:37.340
He's the president of the 
Young Person's Association,

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:41.260
and has been working on local 
revitalization projects for a while now.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:44.760
I pitched the idea of a local 
promotional anime, and they ate it up.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:44.760
<b>Revitalizing the town through animation!!</b>

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:44.760
<b>• Tsubame Mizusaki will be involved
 • Entertain kids
 • Make it an event for the
 shopping district
 • Voice acting auditions
</b>

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:44.760
<b>Fun!</b>

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:46.740
I didn't know Kashimacchy 
was into stuff like that!

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:48.230
That's a crazy coincidence...

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:51.900
Wait, Kanamori, did you take us to 
his shop knowing this would happen?!

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:57.110
All I did was help the two of you brainstorm.

00:18:57.970 --> 00:19:00.110
How is the story progressing?

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:01.850
I'm getting there.

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:04.880
Where's Mizusaki?

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:05.910
Over there.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.030
She said she was working on a 
new model of Adamski saucer.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.670
Let me see the storyboard.

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:25.090
Here's what I've got.

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.570
This is all the direction 
you've given so far?

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:31.220
You're overdoing it again, damn it!

00:19:31.220 --> 00:19:33.770
Quit making extra animation work!

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:36.040
It's already done! It'll be fine!

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:37.170
Get down here, now!

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:39.740
Might need a few adjustments, 
or there could be—

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:40.320
Your little R&D project is canceled!

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.730
It's just gonna get shot down 
by this thing, anyway!

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:59.610
Where's the beam? What about the laser?

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:01.140
Energy weapons weren't originally supposed to be

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:02.530
in the visible spectrum, anyway.

00:20:02.530 --> 00:20:05.860
There's no type of light that just 
zips through the atmosphere like that!

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:09.310
And besides, there are different 
types of directed energy weapons.

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:11.740
It's not all about lasers, y'know!

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:14.610
And even with lasers, they fire 
light at speeds the eye can't track,

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:16.170
for only a fraction of a second,

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:18.380
so it's not gonna look like 
the spotlight at a concert!

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:20.490
Even if it was plasma, there'd be—

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:22.110
You might know what you're saying,

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:24.600
but normal people are
 going to be watching this.

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:25.820
D-Does it not work?

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:27.730
Wh-What the—?!

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:29.540
What's this sound?

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:33.850
I don't really get all the specifics,

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:36.250
but I was imagining this for after the gun fires.

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:39.980
You can hear fans and chains come in contact.

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:41.930
And the rumble is the excitation 
of an electric generator.

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:44.530
This really fits the way 
the concept is conceived.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:47.510
Save the protracted analysis for 
the next time we're getting ramen.

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:49.370
Isn't it rattling a bit too much?

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:50.770
Maybe a bit...

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:52.300
What are you talking about?!

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:54.260
This is how it's supposed to sound!

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:56.050
That's not it, the sound is fine...

00:20:56.050 --> 00:20:59.070
But I was thinking something more like...

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:16.800
Like that!

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:18.220
And what does that mean?

00:21:18.220 --> 00:21:21.260
For the, "Pow!" part, it doesn't 
need any additional sound!

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:24.340
And then no sound after that!

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:27.260
Oh, so that's how you want it performed.

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:28.890
Performed?

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:32.290
What do you think of her take, Doumeki?

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:34.330
I'm not opposed to it.

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:37.100
<i>That's it... It's a performance.</i>

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:41.150
<i>The reason the plane's interior 
was pitch black...</i>

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:45.610
<i>It was to demonstrate how 
vast and bright the sky was.</i>

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:48.820
<i>Everything I've been doing 
so far has been a performance.</i>

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:50.830
<i>It's been that all along...</i>

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:52.810
<i>To depict a vast, unknown world that you</i>

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:54.550
<i>could never grasp from the 
glimpse of a single image...</i>

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:57.980
<i>I've been choosing what 
to draw, and how, all along!</i>

00:21:57.980 --> 00:22:02.150
<i>But I never realized that what 
I was doing was a performance!</i>

00:22:02.150 --> 00:22:04.300
<i>Oh, what bitter fruit my ignorance has borne!</i>

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:06.470
<i>Construction and consistency!</i>

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:08.890
<i>The glory that these factors give rise to!</i>

00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:13.220
Performance will be how I demonstrate 
the greatness of the world I've imagined!

00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:17.590
<i>And with that being the case, 
I must consider the issue further!</i>

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:20.230
I ain't drawing no lasers!

00:22:21.730 --> 00:22:24.190
Down, girl. Let me explain.

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:28.970
Drawing a cannon that doesn't 
emit a beam is important to me.

00:22:29.050 --> 00:22:32.520
Using this cut, you can make it obvious 
that the gun is what shot down

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:34.200
the UFO from their relative positions.

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:37.670
But that's not enough to resolve the issue.

00:22:38.610 --> 00:22:40.870
You think there'll be dissonance 
if there's no beam or bullets involved?

00:22:40.870 --> 00:22:42.050
Wrong!

00:22:42.050 --> 00:22:43.380
Listen up, people...

00:22:43.380 --> 00:22:46.570
"This is a directed energy weapon 
that doesn't project a ray!"

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:50.410
We have to make sure the 
scene conveys that clearly!

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:53.140
In other words, we add a cut that 
makes it obvious something was fired,

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:54.220
even if there was no beam!

00:22:54.220 --> 00:22:57.770
We beef that sucker up with visual cues 
for a massive energy expenditure,

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:00.230
whether it was visible or not!

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:02.810
And we need sound, Doumeki!

00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:08.450
I get how you want the scene performed, 
but what are the UFOs here for?

00:23:08.450 --> 00:23:11.200
Hey, yeah. Who's in them?

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:13.270
That... I am not sure about, yet.

00:23:13.270 --> 00:23:17.270
Actually, why was the town 
so heavily armed, anyway?

00:23:17.270 --> 00:23:19.110
I'm gonna think that up later, too!

00:23:20.110 --> 00:23:23.580
For now, our goal is to prepare for Comet A...

00:23:24.180 --> 00:23:26.660
By creating the greatest world!

00:24:55.970 --> 00:25:00.250
<b>Illustration by: Mari Motohashi</b>
